dentifying a completed Phase III RCT. Since the text confirms none exist, this specific criterion cannot be met using this material. The gap remains unmet in terms of finding positive evidence, but the question is answered negatively.\n-   **Outline Action:** The planner needs to acknowledge the lack of Phase III data. They might need to look for ongoing Phase III trials (not completed) or rely on Phase II/meta-analysis data as the highest level of evidence currently available.\n\n**Refining Status:**\n-   If the gap question is \"Are there any...\", and the answer is \"No\", is the gap fulfilled?\n-   The success criterion says \"Identification of a completed Phase III RCT...\". This sounds like a requirement to *find* one.\n-   If I say \"Status: unmet\", it implies I haven't found the answer. But I have found the answer (None).\n-   However, the instruction says \"Do not call the whole gap fulfilled while a stated success criterion remains open.\"\n-   If the criterion is \"Identification of...\", and I identify \"None\", have I identified a trial? No.\n-   So Status = **unmet**.\n-   Material Usefulness = **direct**.\n\n**Wait, one nuance:** The text says \"as of late 2025\". The current date in the prompt context might be different, but I must treat the text as the source. The text claims no Phase III trials exist.\n-   I will report this finding.\n-   I will mark status as **unmet** because the success criterion (identifying a trial) is not satisfied.\n-   I will mark material_usefulness as **direct** because it directly addresses the existence question.\n\n**Useful Material:**\n-   The explicit statement: \"However, as of late 2025, no completed Phase III randomized trials have yet confirmed a reproducible survival benefit of microbiome-based interventions in oncology.\"\n-   The summary of Phase I/II trials (FMT, SYNB1891, MRx0518) to show what level of evidence *is* available.\n\n**Auxiliary Material:**\n-   Mechanisms of metabolites (SCFAs, etc.).\n-   Reg